/-!
# Verification of the coset hypotheses in 15.3.48

The normal-core calculation uses the genuine earlier star commutator bound
from 14.1.17(3), as in the proof of 15.3.7. It applies uniformly to both
branches, without a restriction on the three-part of the core residual.
The order-two quotient is central in T/Z and irreducible under L₁T; the
extraspecial side condition is retained in the proof of L₁T ≤ H. The
two-core of the actual quotient H/O₂(H) is also proved trivial.

The remaining generalized-Fitting and R₂ preamble calculations and the
F.9.2 application are still required. This module does not yet assert
15.3.48 as a whole.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed
pp.1141–1142 and pp.317–318.
-/
